(552,1254,'Tumors or cancers of the KIDNEY.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'8775FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(553,1256,'A fatal viral disease caused by rabies virus.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'16651FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(554,1257,'A protozoan disease caused by four species of the genus PLASMODIUM (P. falciparum (MALARIA, FALCIPARUM), P. vivax (MALARIA, VIVAX), P. ovale, and P. malariae) and transmitted by the bite of an infected female mosquito of the genus Anopheles. Malaria is endemic in parts of Asia, Africa, Central and South America, Oceania, and certain Caribbean islands. It is characterized by extreme exhaustion associated with paroxysms of high fever, sweating, shaking chills, and anemia.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'8442FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(555,1260,'The presence of pathogenic microorganisms or their toxins in tissues or in the blood. Systemic disease caused by the spread of the microorganisms via the circulating blood is commonly called SEPTICEMIA. (From Stedman, 25th ed)','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'7984FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(556,1262,'The commonest and least serious of the deep mycoses, characterized by nodular lesions of the cutaneous and subcutaneous tissues. It is caused by inhalation of contaminated dust or by infection of a wound.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'7763FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(557,1265,'A general term describing various dermatophytoses. Specific types include TINEA CAPITIS (ringworm of the scalp), TINEA FAVOSA (of scalp and skin), TINEA PEDIS (athlete&#39;s foot), and tinea unguium (see ONYCHOMYCOSIS, ringworm of the nails). (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'7404FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(558,1266,'Dermatological pruritic lesion in the feet, caused by Trichophyton rubrum, T. mentagrophytes, or Epidermophyton floccosum.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'7401FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(559,1271,'Intestinal infection with amoebae.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'123FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(560,1274,'An acute infectious disease of the central nervous system affecting almost all mammals, including humans. It is caused by a rhabdovirus and usually spread by contamination with virus-laden saliva of bites inflicted by rabid animals. Important animal vectors include the dog, cat, vampire bat, mongoose, skunk, wolf, raccoon, and fox. (From Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'7079FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(561,1276,'Inflammation, often mild, of the conjunctiva caused by a variety of viral agents. Conjunctival involvement may be part of a systemic infection.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'6933FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(562,1277,'A group of viral diseases of diverse etiology but having many similar clinical characteristics; increased capillary permeability, leukopenia, and thrombocytopenia are common to all. Hemorrhagic fevers are characterized by sudden onset, fever, headache, generalized myalgia, backache, conjunctivitis, and severe prostration, followed by various hemorrhagic symptoms. Hemorrhagic fever with kidney involvement is HEMORRHAGIC FEVER WITH RENAL SYNDROME.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'6926FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(563,1278,'Viral infections of the leptomeninges and subarachnoid space. TOGAVIRIDAE INFECTIONS; FLAVIVIRIDAE INFECTIONS; RUBELLA; BUNYAVIRIDAE INFECTIONS; ORBIVIRUS infections; PICORNAVIRIDAE INFECTIONS; ORTHOMYXOVIRIDAE INFECTIONS; RHABDOVIRIDAE INFECTIONS; ARENAVIRIDAE INFECTIONS; HERPESVIRIDAE INFECTIONS; ADENOVIRIDAE INFECTIONS; POLYOMAVIRUS HOMINIS 2 infections; and RETROVIRIDAE INFECTIONS may cause this form of meningitis. Clinical manifestations include fever, headache, neck pain, vomiting, PHOTOPHOBIA, and signs of meningeal irritation. (From Joynt, Clinical Neurology, 1996, Ch26, pp1-3)','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'6920FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(564,1279,'Infections with bacteria of the genus ACTINOMYCES.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'15525FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(565,1283,'Anemia due to depletion of red blood cells following an acute loss of blood through hemorrhage.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'15384FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(566,1284,'Infection with a fungus of the species Cryptococcus neoformans.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'1221FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(567,1285,'Liver abscess caused by ENTAMOEBA HISTOLYTICA.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'15215FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(568,1286,'An acute bacterial infection caused by ingestion of BACILLUS organisms. Carnivores may become infected from ingestion of infected carcasses. It is transmitted to humans by contact with infected animals or contaminated animal products. The most common form in humans is cutaneous anthrax.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'6426FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(569,1287,'Infections by bacteria, general or unspecified.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'6313FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(570,1288,'An infectious disease of the skin caused by a virus of the family Poxviridae and characterized by the appearance of small, pearly, umbilicated papular epithelial lesions containing many inclusion bodies.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'1214FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(571,1289,'Tumors or cancer of the OVARY.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'14770FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(572,1290,'Tumors or cancer of the THYROID GLAND.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'14752FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(573,1291,'A fungal infection that may appear in two forms: 1) a primary lesion characterized by the formation of a small cutaneous nodule and small nodules along the lymphatics that may heal within several months; and 2) chronic granulomatous lesions characterized by thick crusts, warty growths, and unusual vascularity and infection in the middle or upper lobes of the lung.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'14639FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(574,1293,'A form of LEPROSY in which there are clinical manifestations of both principal types (lepromatous and tuberculoid). The disease may shift toward one of these two polar or principal forms.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'14597FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(575,1295,'Sexually transmitted form of anogenital warty growth caused by the human papillomaviruses.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'5922FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(576,1296,'A syndrome produced by severe protein deficiency, characterized by retarded growth, changes in skin and hair pigment, edema, and pathologic changes in the liver, including fatty infiltration, necrosis, and fibrosis. The word is a local name in Gold Coast, Africa, meaning &quot;displaced child&quot;. Although first reported from Africa, kwashiorkor is now known throughout the world, but mainly in the tropics and subtropics. It is considered to be related to marasmus. (From Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'5782FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(577,1298,'A localized infection of mucous membranes or skin caused by toxigenic strains of CORYNEBACTERIUM DIPHTHERIAE. It is characterized by the presence of a pseudomembrane at the site of infection. DIPHTHERIA TOXIN, produced by C. diphtheriae, can cause myocarditis, polyneuritis, and other systemic toxic effects.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'5682FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(578,1299,'Infections or infestations with parasitic organisms. They are often contracted through contact with an intermediate vector, but may occur as the result of direct exposure.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'5676FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(579,1300,'Acute, localized autoinoculable infectious disease usually acquired through sexual contact. Caused by HAEMOPHILUS DUCREYI, it occurs endemically almost worldwide, especially in tropical and subtropical countries and more commonly in seaports and urban areas than in rural areas.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'14187FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(580,1301,'Scaly papule or warty growth, caused by five fungi, that spreads as a result of satellite lesions affecting the foot or leg. The extremity may become swollen and, at its distal portion, covered with various nodular, tumorous, verrucous lesions that resemble cauliflower. In rare instances, the disease may begin on the hand or wrist and involve the entire upper extremity. (Arnold, Odom, and James, Andrew&#39;s Diseases of the Skin, 8th ed, p362)','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'14103FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(581,1302,'Syphilis acquired in utero and manifested by any of several characteristic tooth (Hutchinson&#39;s teeth) or bone malformations and by active mucocutaneous syphilis at birth or shortly thereafter. Ocular and neurologic changes may also occur.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'5483FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(582,1303,'An inflammatory disease of the liver caused by hepatitis C virus lasting six months or more.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'14037FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(583,1304,'Paludisme Falciparum','fr',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'5339FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(584,1304,'Malaria caused by PLASMODIUM FALCIPARUM. This is the severest form of malaria and is associated with the highest levels of parasites in the blood. This disease is characterized by irregularly recurring febrile paroxysms that in extreme cases occur with acute cerebral, renal, or gastrointestinal manifestations.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'5338FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(585,1307,'The lack of sufficient energy or protein to meet the body&#39;s metabolic demands, as a result of either an inadequate dietary intake of protein, intake of poor quality dietary protein, increased demands due to disease, or increased nutrient losses.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'4745FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(586,1308,'Infection with CYTOMEGALOVIRUS, characterized by enlarged cells bearing intranuclear inclusions. Infection may be in almost any organ, but the salivary glands are the most common site in children, as are the lungs in adults.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'13363FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(587,1309,'Infeccion aguda febril','es',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'15962FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(588,1311,'A genus of gram-negative, facultatively anaerobic, rod-shaped bacteria that utilizes citrate as a sole carbon source. It is pathogenic for humans, causing enteric fevers, gastroenteritis, and bacteremia. Food poisoning is the most common clinical manifestation. Organisms within this genus are separated on the basis of antigenic characteristics, sugar fermentation patterns, and bacteriophage susceptibility.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'4687FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(589,1312,'Tumors or cancer of the UTERUS.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'4572FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(590,1313,'An acute form of TUBERCULOSIS in which minute tubercles are formed in a number of organs of the body due to dissemination of the bacilli through the blood stream.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:20',NULL,NULL,'4458FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(591,1314,'A disseminated vesicular-pustular eruption caused by the herpes simplex virus (HERPESVIRUS HOMINUS), the VACCINIA VIRUS, or Varicella zoster (HERPESVIRUS 3, HUMAN). It is usually superimposed on a preexisting, inactive or active, atopic dermatitis (DERMATITIS, ATOPIC).','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'12915FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(592,1315,'A mild, highly infectious viral disease of children, characterized by vesicular lesions in the mouth and on the hands and feet. It is caused by COXSACKIEVIRUSES A.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'12830FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(593,1316,'An acute infection of the skin caused by species of STREPTOCOCCUS. This disease most frequently affects infants, young children, and the elderly. Characteristics include pink-to-red lesions that spread rapidly and are warm to the touch. The commonest site of involvement is the face.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'12764FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(594,1317,'A respiratory infection caused by BORDETELLA PERTUSSIS and characterized by paroxysmal coughing ending in a prolonged crowing intake of breath.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'3947FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(595,1318,'An acute infectious disease caused by YERSINIA PESTIS that affects humans, wild rodents, and their ectoparasites. This condition persists due to its firm entrenchment in sylvatic rodent-flea ecosystems throughout the world. Bubonic plague is the most common form.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'3918FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(596,1319,'A contagious skin disease caused by a parasitic mite (Sarcoptes scabiei) and characterized by intense itching.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'139FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(597,1320,'Tumors or cancer of the either the COLON or RECTUM or both. The most frequent malignant tumor in the United States. Etiological factors which increase the risk of colorectal cancer include chronic ulcerative colitis, familial polyposis of the colon, exposure to asbestos, irradiation of the cervix.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'3782FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(598,1321,'Poisoning caused by ingestion of food harboring species of SALMONELLA. Conditions of raising, shipping, slaughtering, and marketing of domestic animals contribute to the spread of this bacterium in the food supply.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'3581FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(599,1322,'Diseases due to or propagated by sexual contact.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'3500FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(600,1324,'Virus diseases caused by the HERPESVIRIDAE.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'11966FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(601,1325,'A chronic infection of the conjunctiva and cornea caused by CHLAMYDIA TRACHOMATIS.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'3280FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(603,1327,'A principal or polar form of LEPROSY in which the skin lesions are few and are sharply demarcated. Peripheral nerve involvement is pronounced and may be severe. Unlike lepromatous leprosy (LEPROSY, LEPROMATOUS), the lepromin test is positive. Tuberculoid leprosy is rarely a source of infection to others.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'11506FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(605,1330,'Infection with nematodes of the genus ONCHOCERCA. Characteristics include the presence of firm subcutaneous nodules filled with adult worms, pruritus, and ocular lesions.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'11419FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(607,1332,'Tuberculosis of the serous membrane lining the thoracic cavity and surrounding the lungs.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'3144FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(608,1335,'Protozoan infection found in animals and man. It is caused by several different genera of COCCIDIA.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'11176FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(609,1336,'DEF: An acute bacterial lower respiratory tract infection. DESC: Associated with fever, symptoms and signs in the chest and abnormalities on the chest X-ray. REF: Oxford Clinical Medicine.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'1407FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(610,1337,'A malignancy arising in uterine cervical epithelium and confined thereto, representing a continuum of histological changes ranging from well-differentiated CIN 1 (formerly, mild dysplasia) to severe dysplasia/carcinoma in situ, CIN 3. The lesion arises at the squamocolumnar cell junction at the transformation zone of the endocervical canal, with a variable tendency to develop invasive epidermoid carcinoma, a tendency that is enhanced by concomitant human papillomaviral infection. (Segen, Dictionary of Modern Medicine, 1992)','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'14375FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(611,1338,'Sudden and usually momentary cessation of the heart beat. This sudden cessation may, but not usually, lead to DEATH, SUDDEN, CARDIAC.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'14360FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(612,1340,'Shock resulting from diminution of cardiac output in heart disease.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'14354FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(613,1341,'DESC: Meningoencephalitis and/or dementia caused by HIV virus. DESC: Can be caused by infection with Toxoplasmosis Gondii or Cryptococcus neoformans, both potentially treatable. REF: Oxford Clinical Medicine','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'1405FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(614,1342,'Medical problems associated with labor including cephalopelvic disproportion, hemorrhage, FETAL DISTRESS, or other disorders.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'14242FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(615,1343,'Bleeding into a cerebral hemisphere of the brain, including lobar, subcortical white matter, and basal ganglia hemorrhages. Commonly associated conditions include HYPERTENSION; INTRACRANIAL ARTERIOSCLEROSIS; INTRACRANIAL ANEURYSM; CRANIOCEREBRAL TRAUMA; INTRACRANIAL ARTERIOVENOUS MALFORMATIONS; CEREBRAL AMYLOID ANGIOPATHY; and CEREBRAL INFARCTION.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'14226FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(616,1344,'A condition characterized by somnolence or coma in the presence of an acute infection with PLASMODIUM FALCIPARUM (and rarely other Plasmodium species). Initial clinical manifestations include HEADACHES, SEIZURES, and alterations of mentation followed by a rapid progression to COMA. Pathologic features include cerebral capillaries filled with parasitized erythrocytes and multiple small foci of cortical and subcortical necrosis. (From Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, p136)','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'14219FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(617,1344,'Homa kali ya ubongo','sw',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'14220FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(618,1345,'A spectrum of histologic changes in the epithelium of the cervix uteri which may begin as a superficial lesion and progress to invasive carcinoma.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'14203FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(619,1346,'A spectrum of histologic changes in the epithelium of the cervix uteri which may begin as a superficial lesion and progress to invasive carcinoma.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'14202FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(620,1347,'A spectrum of histologic changes in the epithelium of the cervix uteri which may begin as a superficial lesion and progress to invasive carcinoma.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'14201FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(621,1349,'Patient has had a cesarean section procedure in the recent past.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'14193FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(622,1351,'Parenchymatous NEUROSYPHILIS marked by slowly progressive degeneration of the posterior columns, posterior roots, and ganglia of the spinal cord. The condition tends to present 15 to 20 years after the initial infection and is characterized by lightening-like pains in the lower extremities, URINARY INCONTINENCE, ATAXIA, severely impaired position and vibratory sense, abnormal gait (see GAIT DISORDERS, NEUROLOGIC), OPTIC ATROPHY, Argyll-Robertson pupils, hypotonia, hyperreflexia, and trophic joint degeneration (Charcot\'s Joint; see ARTHROPATHY, NEUROGENIC). (From Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, p726)','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'14180FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(623,1353,'A behavior disorder originating in childhood in which the essential features are signs of developmentally inappropriate inattention, impulsivity, and hyperactivity. Although most individuals have symptoms of both inattention and hyperactivity-impulsivity, one or the other pattern may be predominant. The disorder is more frequent in males than females. Onset is in childhood. Symptoms often attenuate during late adolescence although a minority experience the full complement of symptoms into mid-adulthood. (From DSM-IV)','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'14159FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(624,1354,'Disorders of increased melanin pigmentation that develop without preceding inflammatory disease.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'14140FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(625,1356,'An inflammatory process involving the chorion, its fetal blood vessels, the umbilical cord, and the amnion by extension of the inflammation, as the amnion itself has no blood supply. This inflammatory process is potentially fatal to mother and fetus.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'14112FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(626,1357,'Chronic nonsuppurative inflammation of periapical tissue resulting from irritation following pulp disease or endodontic treatment.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'14090FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(627,1358,'Passage of excessively liquid or excessively frequent stools.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'14069FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(628,1359,'Inflammation of the gums.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'14053FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(629,1361,'Disorders characterized by recurrent TICS that may interfere with speech and other activities. Tics are sudden, rapid, nonrhythmic, stereotyped motor movements or vocalizations which may be exacerbated by stress and are generally attenuated during absorbing activities. Tic disorders are distinguished from conditions which feature other types of abnormal movements that may accompany general medical conditions. (From DSM-IV, 1994)','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'14010FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(630,1363,'Inflammatory reaction of the tissues surrounding a tooth (periodontium), usually resulting from the extension of gingival inflammation (gingivitis) into the periodontium. (From Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'13987FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(631,1365,'Inflammation of the tonsils, especially the palatine tonsils. It is often caused by a bacterium. Tonsillitis may be acute, chronic, or recurrent.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'13966FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(632,1368,'Liver disease in which the normal microcirculation, the gross vascular anatomy, and the hepatic architecture have been variably destroyed and altered with fibrous septa surrounding regenerated or regenerating parenchymal nodules.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'13947FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(633,1369,'Infectious condition caused by the protozoal parasite Toxoplasma gondii and occurs in acquired and congenital forms.  This type of infection is limited to the central nervous system, including the brain and spinal fluid.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'992FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(634,1370,'Congenital defect in the upper lip where the maxillary prominence fails to merge with the merged medial nasal prominences. It is thought to be caused by faulty migration of the mesoderm in the head region.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'13930FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(635,1371,'Congenital fissure of the soft and/or hard palate, due to faulty fusion.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'13929FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(636,1372,'Inflamation of the female pelvis-not specified','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'905FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(637,1373,'Diagnosis of pneumocystis pneumonia.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'885FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(638,1374,'Fractures of the femur.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:21',NULL,NULL,'13891FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
