(652,1396,'Congenital malformations of organs or parts.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:22',NULL,NULL,'13646FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(653,1397,'Alterations or deviations from normal shape or size which result in a disfigurement of the foot.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:22',NULL,NULL,'13631FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(654,1398,'Unspecified ingestion, inhalation, or other exposure to a toxic substance','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:22',NULL,NULL,'83FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(655,1402,'A syndrome characterized by cardiac enlargement and congestive heart failure. It probably represents the end result of many forms of myocardial damage produced by a variety of toxic, metabolic, or infectious agents.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:22',NULL,NULL,'13597FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(656,1407,'General term for cysts and cystic diseases of the ovary.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:22',NULL,NULL,'13469FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(657,1408,'A chronic, progressive dermatosis characterized by boardlike hardening and immobility of the affected skin, with visceral involvement, especially of lungs, esophagus, kidneys and heart. It may be accompanied by calcinosis, Raynaud&#39;s phenomenon, and telangiectasis (CREST syndrome). It includes acrosclerosis and sclerodactyly.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:22',NULL,NULL,'13444FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(658,1422,'A form of lupus erythematosus in which the skin may be the only organ involved or in which skin involvement precedes the spread into other body systems. It has been classified into three forms - acute (= LUPUS ERYTHEMATOSUS, SYSTEMIC with skin lesions), subacute, and chronic (= LUPUS ERYTHEMATOSUS, DISCOID).','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:22',NULL,NULL,'13400FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(659,1423,'A hair-containing cyst or sinus, occurring chiefly in the coccygeal region.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:22',NULL,NULL,'13382FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(660,1424,'A true cyst of the pancreas to be distinguished from the much more common PANCREATIC PSEUDOCYST by possessing a mucous epithelial lining. Pancreatic cysts are categorized as congenital, retention, neoplastic, parasitic, enterogenous, or dermoid. Congenital cysts occur more frequently as solitary cysts but may be multiple. Retention cysts are gross enlargements of pancreatic ducts secondary to ductal obstruction. (From Bockus Gastroenterology, 4th ed, p4145)','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:22',NULL,NULL,'13377FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(661,1426,'Infection with CYTOMEGALOVIRUS, characterized by enlarged cells bearing intranuclear inclusions. Infection may be in almost any organ, but the salivary glands are the most common site in children, as are the lungs in adults.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:22',NULL,NULL,'13365FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(662,1427,'Gallbladder or biliary duct problems not specified.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:22',NULL,NULL,'8FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(663,1427,'Ù¾ØªÛ’ Ú©ÛŒ Ø¨ÛŒÙ…Ø§Ø±ÛŒØŒ ØªÙØµÛŒÙ„Ø§Øª Ù…ÙˆØ¬ÙˆØ¯ Ù†ÛÛŒÚº','ur',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:22',NULL,NULL,'18136FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(664,1431,'A false belief regarding the self or persons or objects outside the self that persists despite the facts, and is not considered tenable by one&#39;s associates.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:22',NULL,NULL,'13292FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(665,1432,'A distinct and virulent form of DENGUE characterized by thrombocytopenia and hemoconcentration (grades I and II) and distinguished by a positive tourniquet test. When accompanied by circulatory failure and shock (grades III and IV), it is called dengue shock syndrome. (From Dorland, 28th ed)','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:22',NULL,NULL,'13287FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(666,1433,'A chronic endemic form of hypoplasia of the dental enamel caused by drinking water with a high fluorine content during the time of tooth formation, and characterized by defective calcification that gives a white chalky appearance to the enamel, which gradually undergoes brown discoloration. (Jablonski&#39;s Dictionary of Dentistry, 1992, p286)','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:22',NULL,NULL,'13282FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(667,1434,'An autosomal dominant disorder of tooth development characterized by opalescent dentin resulting in discoloration of the teeth, ranging from dusky blue to brownish. The dentin is poorly formed with an abnormally low mineral content; the pulp canal is obliterated, but the enamel is normal. The teeth usually wear down rapidly, leaving short, brown stumps. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:22',NULL,NULL,'13277FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(668,1435,'A personality disorder characterized by a pervasive and excessive need to be taken care of that leads to submissive and clinging behavior and fears of separation, beginning by early adulthood and present in a variety of contexts. (From DSM-IV, 1994)','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:22',NULL,NULL,'13271FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(669,1436,'State in which an individual perceives or experiences a sensation of unreality concerning the self or the environment; it is seen in disorders such as schizophrenia, affection disorders, organic mental disorders, and personality disorders. (APA, Thesaurus of Psychological Index Terms, 8th ed.)','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:22',NULL,NULL,'13269FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(670,1437,'An affective disorder manifested by either a dysphoric mood or loss of interest or pleasure in usual activities. The mood disturbance is prominent and relatively persistent.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:22',NULL,NULL,'13265FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(671,1440,'A situation in which the level of living of an individual, family, or group is below the standard of the community. It is often related to a specific income level.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:22',NULL,NULL,'13251FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(672,1441,'A repetitive and persistent pattern of behavior in which the basic rights of others or major age-appropriate societal norms or rules are violated. These behaviors include aggressive conduct that causes or threatens physical harm to other people or animals, nonagressive conduct that causes property loss or damage, deceitfulness or theft, and serious violations of rules. The onset is before age 18. (From DSM-IV, 1994)','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:22',NULL,NULL,'13250FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(673,1443,'A cognitive disorder marked by an impaired ability to comprehend or express language in its written or spoken form. This condition is caused by diseases which affect the language areas of the dominant hemisphere. Clinical features are used to classify the various subtypes of this condition. General categories include receptive, expressive, and mixed forms of aphasia.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:22',NULL,NULL,'13247FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(674,1444,'Diabetes mellitus characterized by insulin deficiency, sudden onset, severe hyperglycemia, rapid progression to ketoacidosis, and death unless treated with insulin. The disease may occur at any age, but is most common in childhood or adolescence.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:22',NULL,NULL,'13228FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(675,1445,'A heterogeneous group of disorders that share glucose intolerance in common.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:23',NULL,NULL,'13227FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(676,1446,'Protrusion of some part of the abdominal or retroperitoneal structures through the diaphragm into the thorax. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:23',NULL,NULL,'13193FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(677,1447,'Passage of excessively liquid or excessively frequent stools.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:23',NULL,NULL,'13187FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(678,1448,'Inability to urinate. The etiology of this disorder includes obstructive, neurogenic, pharmacologic, and psychogenic causes.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:23',NULL,NULL,'13181FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(679,1449,'A visual symptom in which a single object is perceived by the visual cortex as two objects rather than one. Disorders associated with this condition include REFRACTIVE ERRORS; STRABISMUS; OCULOMOTOR NERVE DISEASES; TROCHLEAR NERVE DISEASES; ABDUCENS NERVE DISEASES; and diseases of the BRAIN STEM and OCCIPITAL LOBE.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:23',NULL,NULL,'13149FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(680,1450,'A chronic form of cutaneous lupus erythematosus (LUPUS ERYTHEMATOSUS, CUTANEOUS) in which the skin lesions mimic those of the systemic form but in which systemic signs are rare. It is characterized by the presence of discoid skin plaques showing varying degrees of edema, erythema, scaliness, follicular plugging, and skin atrophy. Lesions are surrounded by an elevated erythematous border. The condition typically involves the face and scalp, but widespread dissemination may occur.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:23',NULL,NULL,'13144FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(681,1453,'Harm or hurt to the ankle or ankle joint usually inflicted by an external source.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:23',NULL,NULL,'13126FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(682,1454,'General or unspecified injuries involving the fingers.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:23',NULL,NULL,'13125FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(683,1456,'Injuries to the knee or the knee joint.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:23',NULL,NULL,'13123FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(684,1457,'Partial or complete displacement of a tooth from its alveolar support. It is commonly the result of trauma. (From Boucher&#39;s Clinical Dental Terminology, 4th ed, p312)','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:23',NULL,NULL,'13121FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(685,1465,'A mental state characterized by bewilderment, emotional disturbance, lack of clear thinking, and perceptual disorientation.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:23',NULL,NULL,'13074FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(686,1467,'An imprecise term which may refer to a sense of spatial disorientation, motion of the environment, or lightheadedness.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:23',NULL,NULL,'13033FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(687,1468,'Incomplete transposition of the great vessels in which both the aorta and the pulmonary artery arise from the right ventricle, often associated with a subaortic ventricular septal defect.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:23',NULL,NULL,'13018FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(688,1469,'Death that occurs as a result of anoxia or heart arrest, associated with immersion in liquid.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:23',NULL,NULL,'13011FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(689,1470,'Periods of sleep manifested by changes in EEG activity and certain behavioral correlates; includes Stage 1: sleep onset, drowsy sleep; Stage 2: light sleep; Stages 3 and 4: delta sleep, light sleep, deep sleep, telencephalic sleep.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:23',NULL,NULL,'13009FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(690,1472,'Inflammation of the duodenum (first part of small intestine).','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:23',NULL,NULL,'12982FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(691,1473,'Disorders of speech articulation caused by imperfect coordination of pharnyx, larnyx, tongue, or face muscles. This may result from CRANIAL NERVE DISEASES; NEUROMUSCULAR DISEASES; CEREBELLAR DISEASES; BASAL GANGLIA DISEASES; BRAIN STEM diseases; or diseases of the corticobulbar tracts (see PYRAMIDAL TRACTS). The cortical language centers are intact in this condition. (From Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, p489)','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:23',NULL,NULL,'12978FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(692,1474,'Subjective cutaneous sensations (e.g., cold, warmth, tingling, pressure, etc.) that are experienced spontaneously in the absence of stimulation.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:23',NULL,NULL,'12972FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(693,1476,'Painful sexual intercourse.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:23',NULL,NULL,'12958FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(694,1479,'Does the patient have shortness of breath while doing exercise or any physical activities?','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:23',NULL,NULL,'16185FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(695,1482,'Pain in the ear.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:23',NULL,NULL,'12949FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(696,1484,'Congenital downward displacement of the tricuspid valve with the septal and posterior leaflets being attached to the wall of the right ventricle.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:23',NULL,NULL,'12936FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(697,1486,'Excessive amount of watery fluid accumulated in the intercellular spaces, most commonly present in subcutaneous tissue.','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:23',NULL,NULL,'12909FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(698,1488,'The state of the body in relation to the intake and excretion of water and electrolytes, particularly sodium and potassium. It exists in a metabolic balance internally with BODY FLUID COMPARTMENTS, total BODY WATER, BLOOD VOLUME, EXTRACELLULAR SPACE, etc., externally through sensible and insensible SWEATING. The hypothalamus controls water balance. (Dorland, 27th ed; Mountcastle, Medical Physiology, 14th ed, 1980, p1152)','en',2,'2026-10-08 22:40:23',NULL,NULL,'12883FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
